  "result": "CommonJS order helpers: `calcTotal` sums price×qty, `applyDiscount` applies SAVE10/SAVE20 percentage codes, `averageItemPrice` divides total by count, `formatOrder` renders line items plus discounted total.\n\nBugs:\n1. `orders.js:5` — off-by-one: `i <= items.length` reads `items[length]` (undefined) and throws `TypeError` on every call. Should be `i < items.length`.\n2. `orders.js:20` — division by zero for an empty array returns `NaN` (once bug 1 is fixed); guard with `items.length === 0 ? 0 : …`.\n3. `orders.js:13` — `discounts[code]` inherits `Object.prototype`, so codes like `\"constructor\"` or `\"toString\"` return a function; `total * pct` yields `NaN`. Use `Object.hasOwn(discounts, code)` or a `Map`.",
